# A modal spell with two targets resolves while at least one is legal, and each mode acts on its own (CR 608.2b): Bot1 casts
# Collective Brutality choosing the -2/-2 mode on Bot2's Llanowar Elves and the drain on Bot2, and Bot2 Swords its own Elves in
# response. The Elves is gone, the -2/-2 mode does nothing, but the drain still happens: Bot2 loses 2 and Bot1 gains 2 (Bot2 is at 19: it gained 1 from the Swords, the Elves' power).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Swamp
Collective Brutality
Demonic Tutor
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Pearl
Llanowar Elves
Swords to Plowshares
Forest x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Collective Brutality.Cast
Bot1.Modes(2; 3)
Bot1.Target(Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Demonic Tutor)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Swords to Plowshares.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 22
Bot2.Life = 19
Exile = Llanowar Elves
